lens:
Mobile UX, accessibility and web performance, round 5. I tested as a 360x640 Android shopper in the Instagram in-app browser, and also at 360x600, 360x560, 320x568, 390x664, 390x844, 412x732, 412x846, a height sweep from 640 to 900 at widths 360, 393 and 412, and landscape (640x360, 732x412, 844x390).

Stress cases:
- bottom safe-area insets of 24, 34 and 48 px;
- Android fallback faces (Roboto and Noto Serif through a private fontconfig) with the brand fonts blocked;
- Android Font size at 115%, 130%, 150% and 200%. I emulated it two ways: by scaling every computed size, and, new this round, by scaling the page's nine --t-* type tokens. The token method also scales the after-add card before it measures itself, which is closer to how WebView textZoom behaves;
- WCAG 1.4.12 text spacing.

G3 holds. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-4.jpg and measure.json (05:41:52-56) are newer than prototype.html (05:41:50), and my renders match them. Facts end at 562 and the bar starts at 575, with no console errors. fold-ad.png is byte-identical to fold.png (md5 d4ae18d6), which is the builder's choice.

All eight of my round-4 fixes landed and measure as intended:
- the first-screen column;
- html scroll-padding (0 of 31 tab stops are now obscured, down from 4);
- the dock tests the controls under it;
- the ruler at 320 (11 px labels);
- carousel and slide semantics;
- inert;
- the chip in the first paint;
- the live build notes.

Two round-4 changes made things worse:
(1) The column has a fixed height. When the facts plus the 180 px photo floor do not fit, the facts now paint over the reassurance list (text on text). Before round 4 they pushed the page down instead.
(2) history.scrollRestoration = 'manual' is now global. Back from a set piece's page lands at the top of the PDP instead of at the set.
Three scripted jumps also have no history entry, so Android Back after them leaves the page.

Probes ran over http://127.0.0.1 against an untouched copy (md5 a4a874df, the same as pdp10/proto/prototype.html). Speed was measured with CDP throttling (150 ms RTT, 1.6 Mbps, 4x CPU) at DPR 2 and 3. Fixes 1-6 were built into a separate copy, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r5/proto/variant_all5.html (mkall.py, mkall2.py, mkall3.py, mkall5.py), and checked there:
- its first screen is md5-identical to the prototype at 360x640, 320x568, 412x732 and 360x560;
- axe is clean on load and with the viewer open;
- clicking all 57 controls three times raises no JS error.
The prototype was not edited.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r5/out:
- folds.json and var_folds.json;
- overlap_compare.jpg and ovf_sheet.jpg;
- cmp_folds.jpg, big_sheet.jpg, size_compare.jpg, bag_sheet.jpg and load_strip.jpg;
- interact.json, perf.json and perf_font.json.
The scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r5: ovf.js, ovf2.js, matrix.js, cardscale2.js, docksweep.js, back.js, back2.js, back3.js, pol.js, jumps.js, size.js, vax.js, bag.js, ax.js, big.js, monkey.js, perf4.js, perf5.js and same.js.

score_now is the weighted mean of C1, C2, C12, C13, C14, C15, C16 and C20, the same set as rounds 2-4: 389.5 / 44 = 8.85, reported as 8.8.

criteria.note:
At the design target every item fits on one line:
- the worn hero at 77-387;
- the H1 at 399-427;
- the price with GST and 'Surgical steel, PVD rhodium' at 433-462;
- the ladder at ₹2,159 / ₹1,919 / ₹1,679 at 472-538;
- 'Free insured delivery, est. 18–20 Nov · COD available' at 544-562;
- the bar at 575.

The fact line ends 13 px clear at 360x640, 360x600, 360x560, 320x568, 390x664, 412x732 and 412x846, and 39 px clear at 390x844. It also ends 13 px clear with insets of 24, 34 and 48 px and with the brand fonts blocked (folds.json). No viewport scrolls sideways, even at 200% text.

Round 4's column fixed what it set out to fix:
- at 115% the line is 13 px clear at 360x640 and 320x568;
- the tall-screen sweep (640-900) finds nothing half-cut.

Gap: the column cannot shrink below the 180 px photo floor, so on short phones larger text still pushes COD under the bar. With token-scaled text (matrix.js):
- 360x560 at 115%: 26 px under the bar;
- 360x600 at 130%: 33 px under;
- 360x560 at 130%: 73 px under;
- 320x568 at 130%: 63 px under.
Fix 4 brings the first two cases back to 13 px clear (and the third to 41 px under) and leaves the default untouched.

On load the first screen is clean:
- The hero is the worn bracelet and there is no popup or timer.
- The chip and its inline thumbnail paint at 471 ms with the facts (load_strip.jpg). It was a blank 40x52 frame in round 4.
- '1 / 7' is quiet, and nothing is half-cut on tall screens (sweep: none).

New fault, from round 4's fixed-height .above. When the facts outgrow the column they overflow it and paint over the next section, text on text (overlap_compare.jpg, ovf.js):
- 360x560 at 130%: 46 px of overlap;
- 320x568 at 130%: 36 px;
- 360x600 at 130%: 6 px;
- landscape 640x360: 150 px;
- 732x412: 98 px;
- 844x390: 120 px.
'Free insured delivery…' lands on 'Questions before you buy?', and the price row lands on the WhatsApp links. This is C2's own fail condition. Changing 'height' to 'min-height' removes it, and the first screens stay md5-identical (fix 1).

Minor: the landing JPEG paints as a band at the top of the frame over ivory from 471 to 1229 ms. It never shows a whole soft image first (fix 9).

At the default size the card never reaches the H1 at any viewport:
- full at 85-360 (360x640);
- compact, then no suggestion, then mini as the photo shrinks;
- the dock from about 260 px of scroll;
- no card while a control would sit under it.
It has no timer, the bar reads '✓ Added to bag' for 600 ms, and the badge and live region confirm the add.

With token-scaled text the fit logic holds over the photo (compact without the suggestion at 85-229/232). But at 130% after a 60 px scroll the dock lands at 461-567, over 'Free insured delivery… COD available' and the foot of the ladder, and its heading wraps to two lines (cs2_prototype_360x640_1.3_60.png, docksweep.js). That happens because the dock rule tests controls, and the facts contain none. Fix 5.

fixes.change:
Make scroll restoration manual only while an overlay owns the entry.
- L983 becomes: var SR = 'scrollRestoration' in history;
- In openLayer's else branch, before pushState: if (SR) history.scrollRestoration = 'manual';
- In popstate, after setInert(false) and before the afterClose call: if (SR) history.scrollRestoration = 'auto';

Measured (back2.js and back3.js, bfcache on and off):
- Back from a set piece's page returns to 739 (the set), not 0;
- the bag's policy line still opens the fold with its summary at 86;
- Back from the viewer, the bag and the clip keeps 1500, 900 and 2300.

Every scripted jump becomes something Back undoes.
(a) Size guide opens the ruler in the viewer instead of scrolling to the top:
$('#tosize').addEventListener('click', function () { track('nf_size'); openLayer('viewer', { i: SIZE, play: false }); });
In vfill, before the image branch: else if (i === SIZE) { var fg = slides[SIZE].cloneNode(true); fg.removeAttribute('role'); fg.removeAttribute('aria-roledescription'); fg.removeAttribute('aria-label'); fg.style.cssText = 'width:100%;height:auto;background:none'; d.appendChild(fg); }
The viewer's slide 6 then shows the same ruler and caption as the gallery.
(b) #topolicy: call history.pushState({ nf: 'jump' }, '') before openPolicy().
(c) The bag's policy line: afterClose = function () { history.pushState({ nf: 'jump' }, ''); openPolicy(); };
(d) The card's set links: call history.pushState({ nf: 'jump' }, '') before $('#set').scrollIntoView(…).
No URL changes, so the pixel's URL stays clean. Depends on fix 2's order (restoration back to 'auto' before afterClose).

Measured (jumps.js and pol.js), Back now returns to:
- 1953, with focus on Size guide;
- 300 after Read the policy;
- 400 after the bag's policy line;
- the top after 'See the whole set'.
On the prototype each one left the page.

Add a tight mode that drops the two optional words when the facts and the photo floor cannot share the screen.
CSS: .nf-tight .price .mat, .nf-tight .ship .ins { display: none; }
Script: (function () { var f = document.getElementById('product-facts'), r = document.documentElement, cs = getComputedStyle(r); var fit = function () { r.classList.remove('nf-tight'); var col = innerHeight - parseFloat(cs.getPropertyValue('--hdr')) - parseFloat(cs.getPropertyValue('--bar')) - 13; if (f.offsetHeight + 180 > col) r.classList.add('nf-tight'); }; fit(); addEventListener('resize', fit); if (document.fonts) document.fonts.addEventListener('loadingdone', fit); })();
The material is repeated in the reassurance list and the specs. 'insured' already drops below 350 px.

Measured with token-scaled text (matrix.js), the fact line now ends:
- 360x560 at 115%: 13 px clear (was 26 px under the bar);
- 360x640 at 130%: 13 px clear (was 7);
- 360x600 at 130%: 1 px under (was 33);
- 360x560 at 130%: 41 px under (was 73).
Every default-size first screen is unchanged.

Release the below-the-fold images after the brand fonts land (2.5 s cap), not straight after the hero:
var once = false, late = function () { if (once) return; once = true; release(); };
var afterFonts = function () { if (document.fonts) document.fonts.addEventListener('loadingdone', function () { if (document.fonts.check('500 15px "Cormorant Garamond"')) late(); }); setTimeout(late, 2500); };
then hook afterFonts where release was hooked.

Measured (perf5.js, perf_font.json, two runs): the fonts land at 2.15 s against 2.43 / 2.20 s, LCP is unchanged (1.26-1.28 s), and macro-720 and set-3 arrive by 2.65 s. That is still well before a shopper reaches them at 872 and 1548 px.
